  "notes": "University Park track, Enterprise Risk Management option (the major's other option, Real Estate, has no University Park Suggested Academic Plan on the bulletin \u2014 the standalone Real Estate, B.S. major, REST-2026.json, covers that curriculum instead). Shares the identical First/Second Year Smeal core with every other Smeal major built alongside it. RM 320W (no prereq beyond MATH 110/140 or FIN 301, already done) gates RM 405 and RM 440. 'etm' marks Smeal's Entrance-to-Major courses. Post-parens-fix re-scrape (AND/OR prereq-parsing bug fix) revealed ACCTG 211 and SCM 200 both need MATH 21 (not modeled anywhere in this plan, and the Semester 1 math pick falls through to MATH 110/140, neither of which satisfies it) -- with SCM 200/STAT 200 permanently stuck, RM 320W (needs FIN 301 AND MATH 110/140 AND SCM 200/STAT 200) was also unschedulable, cascading to RM 301/RM 405/RM 440 and RM 475. Added the real MATH 21 chain explicitly: MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), matching the fix used in RM-2026.json. Raised max_credits_per_semester from 17 to 18 to fit the extra 9cr. [RM_BS: ADDITIONAL ELECTIVE fix, 2024] Verified against ugstudents.smeal.psu.edu's real RM_BS Degree Requirements page for 2024-25: the real \"Additional Risk Management Elective Courses\" list for this specific catalog year is BLAW 441, BLAW 497 (Special Topics, offered as \"Insurance Law\"), FIN 406, RM 475, and RM 497 (Special Topics, offered as both \"Employee Benefits and Risk Management\" and \"Analytic Foundation of Health Insurance\" -- same course code either way) -- RM 440 (used in the prior 2022/2023 catalog years) was already dropped by this year, contrary to what this plan previously carried forward unchanged. Known caveat: BLAW 497/RM 497 are generic Special Topics catalog entries (credits default to 1.0 in the scraped catalog); the item's own credits field (3) is what the engine actually uses for this plan, so this is display-only and does not affect scheduling. [Business Breadth fix, RM] Verified against ugstudents.smeal.psu.edu's real RM_BS Degree Requirements page for this catalog year's actual 'Business Breadth' course list (self-excluding RM's own required courses, matching the real per-major list exactly). Previously a 100% unfillable placeholder (no match/options field); now wired via the engine's pattern-slot 'match' mechanism, split so at least one slot requires a real 400-level course (matching the handbook's 'at least 3 credits must be at the 400-level' rule).",
